:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 3'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPTION CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=PANELID CLASS=NAMECL VALUE='CMDRST'.
:KEYL NAME=MENUKEYS.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F16 ACTION='MENU MAJOR'.F16=Major menu
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=CMDRST HELP=HLPCMDRST KEYL=MENUKEYS ENTER='RETURN 1' PANELID=PANELID.Restore Commands
:MENU DEPTH='*' SCROLL=YES OPTIONS=OPTION.Select one of the following:
:MENUGRP.Commands
:MENUI OPTION=1 ACTION='CMD ?RST'.Restore Object  RST
:MENUI OPTION=2 ACTION='CMD ?RSTAPARDTA'.
:MENUI OPTION=3 ACTION='CMD ?RSTAUT'.Restore Authority  RSTAUT
:MENUI OPTION=4 ACTION='CMD ?RSTBLDEVT'.
:MENUI OPTION=5 ACTION='CMD ?RSTBUILDER'.
:MENUI OPTION=6 ACTION='CMD ?RSTCFG'.
:MENUI OPTION=7 ACTION='CMD ?RSTDFROBJ'.
:MENUI OPTION=8 ACTION='CMD ?RSTDLO'.
:MENUI OPTION=9 ACTION='CMD ?RSTHAPCY'.
:MENUI OPTION=10 ACTION='CMD ?RSTLIB'.Restore Library  RSTLIB
:MENUI OPTION=11 ACTION='CMD ?RSTLICPGM'.
:MENUI OPTION=12 ACTION='CMD ?RSTOBJ'.Restore Object  RSTOBJ
:MENUI OPTION=13 ACTION='CMD ?RSTPFRCOL'.
:MENUI OPTION=14 ACTION='CMD ?RSTPRDBPR'.
:MENUI OPTION=15 ACTION='CMD ?RSTSYSINF'.
:MENUI OPTION=16 ACTION='CMD ?RSTS36F'.
:MENUI OPTION=17 ACTION='CMD ?RSTS36FLR'.
:MENUI OPTION=18 ACTION='CMD ?RSTS36LIBM'.
:MENUI OPTION=19 ACTION='CMD ?RSTUSRPRF'.Restore User Profiles  RSTUSRPRF
:EMENUGRP.
:EMENU.
:CMDLINE SIZE=LONG.Selection or command
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=HLPCMDRST.Restore Commands - Help
:P.Restore Commands: every command whose name starts with RST, in name order, with the command name at the right of its row. The option numbers follow the full command set of the systems this one is compatible with, so a blank row is a command this release does not provide.
:P.Type an option number and press Enter to prompt the command, or type a command on the command line. F12 returns to the previous menu, F3 to the menu where you started and F16 to the major command groups.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
